      },
      "text": "THE ECONOMICS OF COUTURE:\n    Revenue: ~$1.5-2B globally (tiny vs global fashion ~$2.5 trillion)\n    Purpose: NOT primarily to make money on clothes\n    → Press and editorial coverage (3-6 shows/year)\n    → Brand elevation (\"if you can afford a Dior dress,\n      you might buy Dior perfume\")\n    → Customer relationship (2,000 clients = high-net-worth\n      maintenance; repeat buyers of accessories/fragrance)\n    Fragrance: Chanel No. 5 alone generates ~$600M/year\n    The runway show is the most expensive advertising campaign\n    in the world"
    },
