      "text": "```\n  CHARLES FREDERICK WORTH (1825-1895):\n    First couturier — invented the role of designer-as-artist\n    English-born; moved to Paris; opened at 7 rue de la Paix (1858)\n    Prior: dressmakers made what clients requested\n    Worth: presented his own designs; clients chose from them\n    → Dress design as creative work, not service\n    Dressed Empress Eugénie and European aristocracy\n    First to show clothes on live models\n    First to put his name in garments (the label)"
    },
