      "text": "CRISTÓBAL BALENCIAGA (1895-1972):\n    \"The master of couture\" — even Chanel called him the only\n    true couturier (she was a dressmaker; he was an architect)\n    Trained in Spain; opened in Paris 1937\n    Engineered silhouette away from body: baby doll, cocoon coat,\n    sack dress — clothes as sculpture\n    Closed house 1968 (refused to go RTW); never reopened in his lifetime\n    Current Balenciaga (Demna Gvasalia): radical reinterpretation"
    },
    {
      "id": "13-FASHION-INDUSTRY.md#019",
