      "text": "SHEIN MODEL (founded 2008, Nanjing; now HQ disputed):\n    Digital-native, no physical stores\n    AI-driven trend identification from social media\n    ~2,000-10,000 new styles PER DAY (not per season — per day)\n    Tiny test batches (100-300 units) → AI-gauged response\n    → Scale only what sells → extremely low markdown rate\n    Direct from Chinese factory to consumer (cross-border ecommerce)\n    US: de minimis exemption (packages <$800 duty-free)\n    Regulatory scrutiny: labor practices, IP theft, data\n    Valuation: ~$66B at 2023 attempted IPO; postponed"
    }
